From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:44:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/79] server: deadline_s ends a reply at its deadline with
 every token and usage

A request may name "deadline_s" (seconds, more than 0, at most 1000000), for
chat and legacy completions. At that time the server cancels the engine
itself, still commits the tokens the engine gives before its finished event,
and labels the reply finish_reason "deadline". The final response keeps
usage and token_ids/token_sha256. A token the engine gives after the
deadline cancel may be EOS, hit a stop string or reach max_tokens; the
reply still ends "deadline". A deadline that passes after the reply already
ended (a stop string's own cancel) is not counted. Without the field
nothing changes.

test-request-deadline-host: through chat.run and through openai.run (chat
and completions, whole and streamed): a forced deadline ends the reply with
finish deadline, the late token, usage and ids; no field and a deadline the
reply never meets give the same reply, token sha and stream choices; 0, -1,
"300", true and 1e7 are refused before the engine.
